1
00:00:00,140 --> 00:00:02,660
So in closing, the office of a director

2
00:00:02,660 --> 00:00:05,100
is one of the high health office, is

3
00:00:05,100 --> 00:00:06,080
not to be taken lightly.

4
00:00:06,520 --> 00:00:08,780
So before you accept your next board seat,

5
00:00:08,900 --> 00:00:10,200
or if you're already sitting on the board,

6
00:00:10,320 --> 00:00:12,180
you want to ask yourself, have I done

7
00:00:12,180 --> 00:00:13,100
my due diligence?

8
00:00:13,300 --> 00:00:16,740
Do I understand the extent of my responsibilities

9
00:00:16,740 --> 00:00:18,120
as a director?

10
00:00:18,640 --> 00:00:21,140
Is this worth taking my reputation for?

11
00:00:21,580 --> 00:00:23,540
And if I'm going to accept the office

12
00:00:23,540 --> 00:00:25,060
of a director, I want to continue in

13
00:00:25,060 --> 00:00:27,120
that office, am I ready to do the

14
00:00:27,120 --> 00:00:27,440
work?

15
00:00:27,960 --> 00:00:29,720
I'm not supposed to take, or I'm not

16
00:00:29,720 --> 00:00:32,400
expected to take all that management sells me

17
00:00:32,400 --> 00:00:33,040
as gospel.

18
00:00:33,480 --> 00:00:35,740
I need to do my research and understand

19
00:00:35,740 --> 00:00:37,960
the business of the company.

20
00:00:38,680 --> 00:00:40,480
The second thing I want to say, if

21
00:00:40,480 --> 00:00:43,460
you're sitting on multiple boards right now, you

22
00:00:43,460 --> 00:00:44,940
have to ask yourself, do you have the

23
00:00:44,940 --> 00:00:48,120
capacity to give your best to all of

24
00:00:48,120 --> 00:00:49,300
the boards on which you're sitting?

25
00:00:49,420 --> 00:00:50,920
So maybe it's time to do an audit

26
00:00:51,400 --> 00:00:52,900
of all the boards you're sitting on.

27
00:00:53,320 --> 00:00:55,500
Which one do you consider to be a

28
00:00:55,500 --> 00:00:55,880
nuisance?

29
00:00:57,120 --> 00:00:59,920
And doesn't give you the fulfilment that you

30
00:00:59,920 --> 00:01:00,440
deserve?

31
00:01:01,140 --> 00:01:04,480
Because you really can't over-stretch yourself and

32
00:01:04,480 --> 00:01:06,280
like I said, there's a term now known

33
00:01:06,280 --> 00:01:07,340
as being over-bordered.

34
00:01:07,820 --> 00:01:10,440
If you're more than, I don't want to

35
